	"_about": "KAISER 3X (BMW X3 M40i): its screens are one material with their own pictures (T_Dashboard_D, 512 px): the cluster across the top (the speed band up the left side of its hexagon, 0 20 40 60 then 100 140 200 260 closer together up the top; the rev band up the right, 0 to 7; both bands a dark red strip inside a bright outline; the speed and mph in the middle-left, a map in the middle, the range, the clock, the gear along the bottom), the climate icons, the iDrive screen at the bottom (its welcome page). Kept as painted and made live: the speed, the mph, the range, the clock and the gear where they're painted, both bands lighting up along their red strips (each point carries its value: at); the iDrive shows its own welcome page for the first seconds after the engine starts (intro), then the centre screen's pages. Pixels of that texture. Its steering wheel's stitching (the rim's and the hub's), left in the body by the model's cut, is moved onto the wheel (wheel_parts), so it turns with the leather.",
